{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/841829-need-help-and-advice-for-a-pvp-session-in-larger-chronicle","id":841829,"title":"Need help and advice for a PvP session (in larger Chronicle)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-04T04:58:36-08:00","id":841829,"title":"Need help and advice for a PvP session (in larger Chronicle)","content":"Hello all,<br /> <br /> So here's the topic :<br /> I am running a very political campaign in a small city in Russia (about 20 Kindred only, so everybody is named and known) with 4 Kindred players, 2 Ghouls players and two extra Promethean players (which are more likely satellite).<br /> <br /> We've played 13 sessions so far, and basically, war is on. We have a full blown crisis. The Daeva Regent has been exposed to the sun by an angry promethean ... on public place : So the mascarade is somewhat broken (not massive, but attracts Hunter) of course the Carthian movement is accused (they actually did captured the regent before) and the Invictus/LeS alliance is largely weakened.<br /> <br /> My players splited in 4 vs 2, 4 Carthians vs 2 Invictus (actually, one L&amp;S priest allied with the Prince Childe)<br /> (they did it themselves, really, no script, it just happened, 2ED is awesome !).<br /> Most of all are neonates.<br /> <br /> So the main point for the two groups is to hurt the other.<br /> My big NPCs are almost all asleep, away, killed or weakened. So it's perfect timing for the Carthians movement to make its moves.<br /> We have a player vs player situation. Which is great.<br /> Get it ? Sorry my english isn't native.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is a new and exciting situation for me, for the next two sessions at least, i won't have to run down a script or to pop events out, because the players themselves will drop event and take action, from which on i will have to react.<br /> <br /> Two sessions, one Carthian, one Feodal (LeS and IN allied).<br /> I assume both side will attempt to do alliance with the non alined covenant and clan (Gangrel and Ordo Dracul)<br /> I assume both side will try to spy on the other side.<br /> I assume (and advice them) than both side will take root in some territory. (we play with the full Damnation City set up)<br /> <br /> <br /> Two major problems pops out :<br /> <br /> 1 - I have to act more as a referee than as a storyteller, and since i am the only GM and that there's a lot of data, my choices might seem unbalanced and unfair. But that's my job. Stick with the logic.<br /> <br /> 2 - Since both team play out within one week of delay, they can not meet, talk (might be on the phone still) and physically attack the other side. Worse : they can not set up a meeting in other to convince someone to betray.<br /> <br /> It happened already once : Live and unexpected treason is very hard to handle as a GM (happened via text : a player text a GM's NPC under the table while smiling to the other player : perfect but chaotic !)<br /> Might be that this situation doesn't last longer than two session after all, they might come to an agreement...<br /> <br /> <br /> I am all hears to any advice, experience and thoughts on how to handle this exciting situation !<br /> Really, i feel pretty lost, and i would like to offer to my players the best PvP experience possible.<br /> Vampire is a good political game, it had to run down like this ... now it's war, the danse macabre is over.<br /> The time for Elyson speach and voiled threats is done.<br /> <br /> And oh, i forgot to mention,<br /> Two owls have been seen in town.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6461,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6461-essen_ko","user":"essen_ko","date":". 03-04-2016, 08:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6461-essen_ko","name":"essen_ko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6461_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T05:09:23-08:00","id":841833,"title":"","content":"PS : i am not looking for tricks or idea on &quot;what&quot; could happen, since they will do most of the job<br /> but for tricks and idea on &quot;how&quot; this might happen and &quot;how&quot; to run this session down. This is more of a technical problem. I am looking to solve a gameplay issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6461,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6461-essen_ko","user":"essen_ko","date":". 03-04-2016, 08:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6461-essen_ko","name":"essen_ko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6461_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T05:32:14-08:00","id":841841,"title":"","content":"About political traechery and plotting against themselfs, talking from a personal experience, I have noted the importance of some major NPCs (The Prince, the Judex, the Kogaion, etc).<br /> The players will probably not only step on the toes of each other, but on the toes of some important NPCs. I tend to not use the NPCs to end physical conflict, unless the players have tried to specifically injure that NPC, but they can provide resources, information, etc.<br /> This 2nd E is awesome for social maneuvers, theres a lot of Merits that can be used to undermine the Merits of other characters.<br /> If it scalate to physical, I don't think that physical combat is something complicated, if both parts have agreed and know that maybe one of them can/will lose the character.<br /> <br /> So, to resume, here is a list of a few tricks that I would use:<br /> - Make NPCs interfere sometimes, to help or to hinder.<br /> - Try to work on the objectives of the neutral factions(Ordo Dracul), that way, you can define who has most chances of sucess for an alliance.<br /> - Not only the PCs can use the treachery card, some NPCs might do that as well if they personal objectives align better with other factions, after all, they are at war, that's the right time to pull this card.<br /> - The owls are a great plus to the situation. Possession and stuff. They can help the faction that has more chance of wiping the other, juts to help to eliminate some Kindred. Use this if you can.<br /> <br /> About the point you raised on 1, why your choices might seem umbalanced?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T09:03:10-08:00","id":842595,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/841829-need-help-and-advice-for-a-pvp-session-in-larger-chronicle?p=841841#post841841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have noted the importance of some major NPCs (The Prince, the Judex, the Kogaion, etc).</div> </div> </div> </div>Like Primogenes or Harpies. What is a Judex ? <br /> Is Kogaion the Ordo Dracul leader ? In town we have a Voivode Lord (from 2ED scale's)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/841829-need-help-and-advice-for-a-pvp-session-in-larger-chronicle?p=841841#post841841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Try to work on the objectives of the neutral factions(Ordo Dracul), that way, you can define who has most chances of sucess for an alliance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes the is the key point, since neutral factions will actually &quot;choose&quot; who's gonna make it.<br /> There will be important roleplay work for both team trying to rally them, with lies and big arguments.<br /> For this, i am using a strange mechanic : in the computer game Crusarder Kings II (which involes some RPG gameplay if you know) the characters have an opinion about others rated from -100 to +100. Example : I like him +50 because we are friend (+50), we performed a dangerous action as allies (+30) but we are from different clan (-10) and he hid important secrets to me (-20) = +50<br /> Or : I like her -45 because she's from an other covenant (-15), we are from different clan (-10), we share different views about traditions (-10) and i am neonate and she's ancillae (-10) = -45<br /> Of course this goes both ways which might be different. Leading to some interesting and CLEAR situations.<br /> <br /> With this, i know the relationships between all PCs and NPCs and everybody might act logically.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/841829-need-help-and-advice-for-a-pvp-session-in-larger-chronicle?p=841841#post841841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- The owls are a great plus to the situation. Possession and stuff. They can help the faction that has more chance of wiping the other, juts to help to eliminate some Kindred. Use this if you can.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's only be rumors about them till now. Some characters saw one of them, shortly.<br /> Actually, i dont really know what to do with Owls. I've red the Parliament of Owls, which was an awesome chapter, but i don't really get what THEY want, what's their plan. Except taking pleasure spreading complete chaos. Which is more the task of my political malchavians actually.<br /> What do you do with owls ? How do play them ? Do they teamwork ?<br /> I understand a big theme is paranoia, everybody suspecting anyone to be one of them.<br /> Any good gameplay experience with the strix ?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo;n841841[FONT=inherit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the point you raised on 1, why your choices might seem umbalanced?[/FONT]</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><br /> Because I see my self as some kind of master of ceremony whose role is to assure great fun to everyone, and that doing so makes me willing to me nice to some players, and has consequences on the others, especially the more experienced ones who take greater risks. Leading to -- very exgerated : &quot;Sorry, what you are doing is not working because it goes against another player that the GM wants to help&quot;.</span><br /> <br /> Thanks for answering !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6461-essen_ko","name":"essen_ko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6461_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T14:00:31-08:00","id":842715,"title":"","content":"&lt;&lt; What is a Judex ? &gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> Judex (Latin for judge) In first edition VtR, it was a single member of the Invictus appointed by the Inner Circle or the previous acting Judex to act as mediator of disputes between Invictus members. Usually it was someone the prior Judex or Inner Circle appointed because the individual had already established a reputation for being dispassionate and/or impartial in their dealings with others. It's become a throwaway reference to whomever the Invictus publicly acknowledges as their covenant leader or the oldest Invictus member who is seeking praxis in a domain that doesn't have an Invictus prince.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T17:40:02-08:00","id":842803,"title":"","content":"Judex is an important member of the Invictus. Kogaion is the leader of the Ordo Dracul in a domain.<br /> <br /> About the Owls, they seem to want to spread caos and destruction. Some of them are lonely antagonist, but some like to move in groups.<br /> You can use them for whatever you want. That's the beauty of them as antagonists, you can do whatever you like. Some of them will help or make pacts with players and NPC, and others just want to see the Kindred burn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}